-- title:
--   Connected–étale splitting of a p-divisible tower over Fₚ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $h$ a natural number, and let $G$ be a family of commutative rings $G(v)$, $v \in \mathbb{N}$, each carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbf{F}_p = \mathbb{Z}/p$ that is cocommutative and finite as a $\mathbf{F}_p$-module, equipped with bialgebra maps $s_v \colon G(v+1) \to G(v)$ that are surjective, with $\dim_{\mathbf{F}_p} G(v) = p^{vh}$ for all $v$, and with $\ker s_v$ equal to the $p^v$-torsion ideal of $G(v+1)$, that is, the ideal generated by the image of the augmentation ideal $\ker \varepsilon$ under the algebra map $[p^v]$ obtained as the $p^v$-th convolution power of the identity. Then there exist natural numbers $h_c, h_e$ with $h_c + h_e = h$ and two further such families $Gc$, $Ge$ (commutative rings, cocommutative Hopf algebras over $\mathbf{F}_p$, finite over $\mathbf{F}_p$) with bialgebra transition maps $sc_v$, $se_v$, together with bialgebra maps $qc_v \colon G(v) \to Gc(v)$, $\pi e_v \colon G(v) \to Ge(v)$, $\sigma_v \colon Ge(v) \to G(v)$ and $\Theta_v \colon G(v) \to Gc(v) \otimes_{\mathbf{F}_p} Ge(v)$, such that: every $Gc(v)$ is a local ring, every $Ge(v)$ is reduced and formally unramified over $\mathbf{F}_p$; each of $Gc$ and $Ge$ satisfies the same three tower conditions as $G$ (surjective transitions, $\dim_{\mathbf{F}_p} Gc(v) = p^{v h_c}$, $\dim_{\mathbf{F}_p} Ge(v) = p^{v h_e}$, and kernel of the transition at level $v$ the $p^v$-torsion ideal); $qc_v$ and $\pi e_v$ are surjective, $\ker \pi e_v$ is the nilradical of $G(v)$, $\pi e_v \circ \sigma_v = \mathrm{id}$, and $\ker qc_v$ is the ideal of $G(v)$ generated by $\sigma_v(\ker \varepsilon_{Ge(v)})$; $\Theta_v$ is bijective and is given on elements by $b \mapsto (qc_v \otimes \pi e_v)(\Delta b)$; and the four squares $qc_v \circ s_v = sc_v \circ qc_{v+1}$, $\pi e_v \circ s_v = se_v \circ \pi e_{v+1}$, $s_v \circ \sigma_{v+1} = \sigma_v \circ se_v$, $\Theta_v \circ s_v = (sc_v \otimes se_v) \circ \Theta_{v+1}$ commute.
--
--   This is the connected–étale decomposition of a $p$-divisible group over the prime field, written levelwise on coordinate rings and made compatible with the transition maps, so that both factors are again $p$-divisible towers with heights adding to $h$. It is used in the construction of Honda systems and split coordinates, in the analysis of Néron objects attached to modular curves at $p$, and in the level-one Cartier-dual splitting statement.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_PDivisibleGroup_exists_tower_isLocalRing_isReduced_bijective_tensorProduct_comul_zmodp.lean

import Mathlib
